	quest.1A1320A96D2E14F3.quest_subtitle: "Extras: Misc"
	quest.1A1320A96D2E14F3.title: "Ionic Membrane Upgrade"
	quest.1A1B057049B2AB58.quest_desc: ["The crafting core is used to craft several end-game items. See all uses in JEI."]
	quest.1A1B057049B2AB58.quest_subtitle: "Extended Crafting"
	quest.1A22932E319FCC59.quest_desc: ["The §6Mechanical Press§r above a Basin compacts ingots into plates and crushed ores into sheets. The press also runs deploying recipes."]
	quest.1A22932E319FCC59.quest_subtitle: "Create"
	quest.1A320CBEE5D63B6B.quest_desc: ["The frame blocks that form the fusion sphere."]
	quest.1A320CBEE5D63B6B.quest_subtitle: "Reactors"
	quest.1A320CBEE5D63B6B.title: "Fusion Reactor Frame"
	quest.1A378D0D3AA38021.quest_desc: ["A unique crafting method of Powah, uses items and energy to craft recipes"]
	quest.1A3B93ADCE8E38D6.quest_desc: ["A panel on a cable that displays a variable's value. Text, numbers, items or fluids."]
	quest.1A3B93ADCE8E38D6.quest_subtitle: "Integrated Dynamics"
	quest.1A40E97E9775C979.title: "Jet Suit"
	quest.1A4758DDB7A6D5D7.quest_desc: ["Steel tier helmet from Mekanism Tools."]
	quest.1A4758DDB7A6D5D7.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism Tools"
	quest.1A4758DDB7A6D5D7.title: "Steel Helmet"
	quest.1A518FF85B798517.quest_desc: [
		"Aura and its presence in the world has been a conundrum to researchers for a long time now. Back in the day, they used to use Bottles to collect aura and to be able to analyze it in greater detail as it becomes visible to the naked eye that way. Soon after, complaints from uninformed civilians started troubling them: \"Other scientists already have a use for bottles, this will cause issues\", they said."
		""
		"As such, and to shut out all the incoherent blabber, they created the Bottle and Cork: A similar, yet slightly different utensil to the bottle that can be used exclusively to collect aura by simply interacting with the air while holding it."
		""
		"Refer to the Book of Natural Aura (guidebook) for full detailed information on Nature's Aura."
	]
	quest.1A5C0D96992297B5.quest_desc: ["Where you create new Glyphs and write spells onto Spell Parchment and Caster Tomes. Drop the reagent and Source on it to unlock a glyph."]
	quest.1A5C0D96992297B5.quest_subtitle: "Ars Nouveau"
	quest.1A697CB0864BFBB7.quest_desc: ["Refined Obsidian tier shield from Mekanism Tools."]
	quest.1A697CB0864BFBB7.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism Tools"
	quest.1A697CB0864BFBB7.title: "Refined Obsidian Shield"
	quest.1A744101DF060973.quest_desc: ["§6Absolute Enriching Factory§r. Processes many items at once. Higher tiers add more slots and speed."]
	quest.1A744101DF060973.quest_subtitle: "Extras: Factories"
	quest.1A744101DF060973.title: "Absolute Enriching Factory"
	quest.1A9B78F321A4D3B8.quest_desc: ["§6Verdium Miner§r, tier §e4§r of §e8§r. Build its frame from the previous tier, then assemble the miner to pull §bVerdium§r and other resources from the void."]
	quest.1A9B78F321A4D3B8.quest_subtitle: "Void Miners"
	quest.1A9B78F321A4D3B8.title: "Verdium Miner"
	quest.1AA81BAD36C2CF83.quest_desc: ["The §6Portable Energy Storage§r buffers RF for your early grid. Crafted from a Basic Battery, Nickel, Coil and Silicon."]
	quest.1AA81BAD36C2CF83.quest_subtitle: "Oritech"
	quest.1AB411A0EA12469E.quest_desc: ["The §6Hose Pulley§r drains or fills entire lakes by lowering a hose. Pair with a tank for industrial fluid handling."]
	quest.1AB411A0EA12469E.quest_subtitle: "Create"
	quest.1AB8244D9A52E7F4.quest_desc: ["Crafted using the energizing orb. Used in crafting recipes for hardened tier Powah items."]
	quest.1ACDC1DD15782D56.quest_desc: ["Craft a §6Dank§r, a portable storage device that holds many stacks of dozens of item types in one compact inventory. Tier §e1§r is modest, but it scales fast."]
	quest.1ACDC1DD15782D56.quest_subtitle: "Dank Storage"
	quest.1ACDC1DD15782D56.title: "Pocket Storage"
	quest.1AD20EA728CB95A7.quest_desc: ["§6Absolute Stamping Factory§r. An Extras-only factory type, available in the four highest tiers."]
	quest.1AD20EA728CB95A7.quest_subtitle: "Extras: Factories"
	quest.1AD20EA728CB95A7.title: "Absolute Stamping Factory"
	quest.1AD67DAA84745357.quest_desc: ["The §6Industrial Chiller§r produces cold fluids and is a prerequisite for nuclear reactor cooling loops."]
	quest.1AD67DAA84745357.quest_subtitle: "Oritech"
	quest.1ADD76E7FE86DE57.quest_desc: ["§6Infinite Combining Factory§r. Processes many items at once. Higher tiers add more slots and speed."]
	quest.1ADD76E7FE86DE57.quest_subtitle: "Extras: Factories"
	quest.1ADD76E7FE86DE57.title: "Infinite Combining Factory"
	quest.1AE2DA480EB23947.quest_desc: ["Used to make plastic. Refer to JEI and the manual."]
	quest.1AE506C74AF7D407.quest_desc: ["The best draconic scientists have figured out a way to duplicate chaos shards. Breaking down a chaos shard into its tiniest fragments will allow you to transform it into something that can be refined to create large chaos fragments."]
	quest.1B0C64ADE307447B.quest_desc: ["Places blocks in a Line (7 or 21) or Area (7x7 or 21x21). Sneak-right-click air to change mode. Sneak-right-click your last placement to undo."]
	quest.1B0C64ADE307447B.quest_subtitle: "BetterBlockz"
	quest.1B146007CA8A3052.quest_desc: [
		"There is only one type of rocket in Stellaris; you can improve your rocket using various upgrades."
		""
		"Make sure you only take off in your rocket from the overworld (the dimension where you started the pack) or the planets! Otherwise, messy things can happen!"
	]
	quest.1B17A64C7D6C88F7.quest_desc: ["Transmit power wirelessly to charge items in your inventory!"]
	quest.1B1E9AFA7D0B0970.title: "Upgrades"
	quest.1B4A6ACF29C9DD46.quest_desc: ["The §6Combiner§r allows the player to create an ore block from 8 dust. Place the ore dust in the top slot, and some cobblestone in the bottom slot, and it will combine to make the ore block. It requires 1000 power per operation. Works with the dust of copper, iron, tin, osmium, obsidian (only needs 4) and gold. Also allows 1 Flint to a gravel block and 16 Redstone/Lapis to their ores."]
	quest.1B5C8B86CFDBB051.quest_desc: [
		"For quest completions, items are automatically detected when they are in your inventory. Make sure to hold completed items in your inventory until FTB Quests detects it -> no quest complete = no rewards!"
		""
		"Quest rewards include coins. Coins can be redeemed at the coin shop for reward bags!"
		""
		"Click on an item in your quest book or search in JEI to find how to craft items. You can also press \"r\" while hovering over an item. Press \"u\" to see an item's uses."
		""
		"You can \"twerk\" to grow trees and some crops (pressing shift multiple times - make sure sticky keys are disabled on a PC), and you can vein mine blocks (the mod is FTB Ultimine, default keybind is the grave key `)."
		""
		"To gain more than the five base hearts, try eating a wide variety of food! (You will get your first extra heart after eating 10 unique foods)"
		""
		"You do not have to complete a whole page of quests before moving on to the next, but note that some quests cannot be started without finishing others first."
	]
	quest.1B5C8B86CFDBB051.quest_subtitle: "Important Info Here!"
	quest.1B6FEBB8D9440617.quest_desc: ["Can be hammered into dust. Use in a sieve to obtain resources!"]
	quest.1B940854A058386C.quest_desc: ["Converts organic materials into biomass fuel"]
	quest.1BAB46320F75A91B.quest_desc: [
		"When starting out as a magical botanist, it proves beneficial to use the powers of nature on a more direct level before delving directly into aura itself. The Ritual of the Forest uses properties of Gold Powder to incorporate the power of natural ingredients directly into a fresh, growing tree, devouring it in the process, but at the same time, transforming it into useful tools and items."
		""
		"To construct this ritual, one has to place Gold Powder in the configuration shown in the guidebook, with some Wooden Stands around that which will hold the ingredients. Then, the correct sapling must be placed in the middle, and, either through some kind of fertilizer, or through the inevitability of time, its growth will cause the ritual to start. Note that care needs to be taken as rituals require specific types of saplings."
		""
		"Refer to the Book of Natural Aura (guidebook) for full detailed information on Nature's Aura."
	]
	quest.1BAB46320F75A91B.title: "Ritual of the Forest"
	quest.1BCBD9BB772CB432.quest_desc: ["Crafts the Extended devices that are too complex for a crafting table, and runs in-world transforms like fluix. §eIts screen face cannot connect to a network.§r"]
	quest.1BCBD9BB772CB432.quest_subtitle: "ExtendedAE"
	quest.1BDB27BEE2F15015.quest_desc: ["§6Advanced Bin§r. Bulk single-item storage block."]
	quest.1BDB27BEE2F15015.quest_subtitle: "Extras: Storage"
	quest.1BDB27BEE2F15015.title: "Advanced Bin"
	quest.1BDB8EDBC8F52E9E.quest_desc: ["While bearing some similarity to Fluix ME Covered Cable in appearance, they provide diagnostic function by visualizing the channel usage on the cables, the channels appear as lit colored lines that run along the black stripe on the cables giving you an understanding of how your channels are being used on your network. For regular smart cables, the first four channels show as lines matching the color of the cable, the next four show as white lines. For dense smart cable, each stripe represents 4 channels."]
	quest.1C06B9727A06A7D8.quest_desc: [
		"Crafting CPUs are multiblocks, and must be solid rectangular prisms with no gaps. They are made out of several components."
		""
		"Each CPU must contain at least 1 crafting storage block (and the minimum viable CPU is in fact just a single 1k crafting storage)."
		""
		"Crafting storages are available in all the standard cell sizes (1k, 4k, 16k, 64k, 256k). They store the ingredients and intermediate ingredients involved in a craft, so larger or more storages are required for the CPU to handle crafting jobs with more ingredients."
	]
	quest.1C151667128F6018.quest_desc: ["Bend physics in the Antimatter chamber and bottle 64 pellets."]
	quest.1C151667128F6018.quest_subtitle: "Master"
	quest.1C151667128F6018.title: "Impossible Material"
	quest.1C2CF2302444D13A.quest_desc: ["§6Reinforced Alloy§r (Infused Alloy and diamond). Gates Elite machines."]
	quest.1C2CF2302444D13A.quest_subtitle: "Alloys"
	quest.1C2CF2302444D13A.title: "Reinforced Alloy"
	quest.1C30D7DF9779DD9C.quest_desc: ["A machine that grinds items like ores into dusts, providing basic ore doubling."]
	quest.1C3512BA7B488C67.quest_desc: [
		"Note: Most machines in the Mekanism mod can be upgraded into factories."
		""
		"The Metallurgic Infuser is the first step in the Mekanism tech tree. The Metallurgic Infuser is a machine used in the production of Steel Ingots, Bronze Ingots, Enriched Alloy, and Obsidian Ingots."
	]
	quest.1C415F1269D75A95.quest_desc: ["Caps a fuel assembly and lets you throttle the reaction."]
	quest.1C415F1269D75A95.quest_subtitle: "Reactors"
	quest.1C415F1269D75A95.title: "Control Rod Assembly"
	quest.1C707A653F0D6D54.quest_desc: [
		"No restrictions, unlimited durability."
		""
		"Right-click a block with a wand → it becomes an Enlivened Block entity."
		""
		"Enlivened entities can be captured/duplicated by other mods , providing a renewable source of that block. Note: Does not work if the spawner does not copy NBT."
		""
		"Use a Mob Imprisonment Tool on your new entity and duplicate in the Industrial Foregoing Mob Duplicator."
	]
	quest.1C7F8D15A8752223.quest_desc: ["Craft an §6Illuminant Block§r from stone, glowstone, and redstone. Simply Light's bright, even panels light any interior without a torch in sight."]
