	quest.4A48C9233678C0E2.title: "Osmium Helmet"
	quest.4A7914DE1EE8C228.quest_desc: ["§6Pink EMC Link§r, tier §e5§r of §e16§r. EMC Links import and export items, fluids and raw EMC, the backbone of EMC automation."]
	quest.4A7914DE1EE8C228.quest_subtitle: "Project Expansion: EMC Links"
	quest.4A7914DE1EE8C228.title: "Pink EMC Link [MK 5]"
	quest.4A896062318A7D4A.quest_desc: ["Spooky Scary Skeletons Send Shivers Down My Spine!"]
	quest.4A94EFEE171A8EAC.quest_desc: [
		"The molecular assembler takes items input into it and carries out the operation defined by an adjacent ME Pattern Provider, or the inserted Crafting Pattern, Smithing Table Pattern, or Stonecutting Pattern, then pushes the result to adjacent inventories."
		""
		"However, their main use is next to a ME Pattern Provider. Pattern providers have special behavior in this case, and will send information about the relevant pattern along with the ingredients to adjacent assemblers. Since assemblers auto-eject the results of crafts to adjacent inventories (and thus into the return slots of the pattern provider), an assembler on a pattern provider is all that is needed to automate crafting patterns."
	]
	quest.4A97D4D54CD232BF.quest_desc: ["Transmits energy through the cable, upgradable."]
	quest.4A9E341B69EDA897.quest_desc: ["The §6Particle Accelerator Speed Sensor§r reports particle velocity to the controller."]
	quest.4A9E341B69EDA897.quest_subtitle: "Oritech Things"
	quest.4AB396AED180FC43.quest_desc: ["The §6Mechanical Bearing§r rotates an attached contraption around its axis. The base of windmills, train turntables, and rotating bridges."]
	quest.4AB396AED180FC43.quest_subtitle: "Create"
	quest.4AB667CCE02BE8CA.quest_desc: ["A ritual that generates stone and ore-bearing rock in its area."]
	quest.4AB667CCE02BE8CA.quest_subtitle: "Ars Caelum"
	quest.4ADC75DE70AEE87C.quest_desc: ["Slay a shulker in an End City to obtain."]
	quest.4ADFC70E3DA60950.quest_desc: [
		"A device to extract Alchemical Salt from items."
		""
		"Place the oven on top of the braizer. Fill the braizer with blaze rods to heat the oven!"
		""
		"See The Hermetica for more details on Theurgy."
	]
	quest.4AEC1E7CE3F054B7.quest_desc: [
		"Break a block with a hammer to crush it. Cobblestone -> Gravel, Gravel -> Sand, Sand -> Dust, Netherrack -> Crushed Netherrack, End Stone -> Crushed End Stone, Cobbled Deepslate -> Crushed Deepslate, Blackstone -> Crushed Blackstone, Crushed Netherrack -> Red Sand. Later, you can automate this process with different machines. For now, vein mining and construction sticks will be your friend. "
		""
		"Try hammering logs to obtain wood chippings - great for compost!"
	]
	quest.4AF7ACF846C43CCB.quest_desc: ["§6Caerium Modifiers§r. Slot these into a Caerium Miner to tune it: §eEnergy§r lowers power draw, §eItem§r boosts output, §eSpeed§r runs it faster. Craft all three for tier §e6§r."]
	quest.4AF7ACF846C43CCB.quest_subtitle: "Void Miners"
	quest.4AF7ACF846C43CCB.title: "Caerium Modifiers"
	quest.4B06F197D8757873.quest_desc: ["The §6Engineer's Goggles§r reveal stress, RPM, and contraption details when worn. The essential debugging tool."]
	quest.4B06F197D8757873.quest_subtitle: "Create"
	quest.4B22EF984AA9E58E.quest_subtitle: "Advanced AE"
	quest.4B49091675AA1DFA.quest_desc: ["Any item placed into its inventory will be converted into EMC and will transfer energy from Energy Collectors to Energy Condensers. When transferring, it gives a 10 EMC per second bonus. It will charge any of the Klein Star series with EMC. "]
	quest.4B4F025A5D54F8D6.quest_desc: ["§6Elite Injecting Factory§r. Processes many items at once. Higher tiers add more slots and speed."]
	quest.4B4F025A5D54F8D6.quest_subtitle: "Extras: Factories"
	quest.4B4F025A5D54F8D6.title: "Elite Injecting Factory"
	quest.4B5873D3379CB4B5.quest_desc: ["§6Infinite Bin§r. Bulk single-item storage block."]
	quest.4B5873D3379CB4B5.quest_subtitle: "Extras: Storage"
	quest.4B5873D3379CB4B5.title: "Infinite Bin"
	quest.4B5D653985BDC839.quest_desc: [
		"Together with the ritual, knowledge of Tokens can be gained: Wooden figurines, depicting key emotions - created from trees infused with their respective symbols. These figurines contain a combination of the vast power of aura itself and the power of the emotions they represent. Going forward, these Tokens will be a key construction ingredient."
		""
		"Refer to the Book of Natural Aura (guidebook) for full detailed information on Nature's Aura."
	]
	quest.4B62DEDA4F901770.quest_desc: ["Maximize smelting efficiency with unparalleled speed, reconfigurable sides, augments for smoking and blasting, and much more."]
	quest.4B7A9E79D4CAE2E1.quest_desc: ["Steel tier shovel from Mekanism Tools."]
	quest.4B7A9E79D4CAE2E1.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism Tools"
	quest.4B7A9E79D4CAE2E1.title: "Steel Shovel"
	quest.4B893A1BDA3CEC33.quest_desc: ["A powerful sword in it's own right by charging it and using activating it (C) the §6Dark Matter Sword§r will consume EMC in exchange for a devastating sweep attack. The area of the attack is controlled by charge level (V, shift+V)."]
	quest.4B8B7DFAE855A0E2.quest_desc: ["§6Shining Alloy§r. An Extras crafting alloy."]
	quest.4B8B7DFAE855A0E2.quest_subtitle: "Extras: Misc"
	quest.4B8B7DFAE855A0E2.title: "Shining Alloy"
	quest.4B93E6027F503503.quest_desc: ["Quantum armor card granting §bcreative-style flight§r."]
	quest.4B93E6027F503503.quest_subtitle: "Advanced AE"
	quest.4BA31070C50306EF.quest_desc: ["§6Basic Infusing Factory§r. Processes many items at once. Higher tiers add more slots and speed."]
	quest.4BA31070C50306EF.quest_subtitle: "Extras: Factories"
	quest.4BA31070C50306EF.title: "Basic Infusing Factory"
	quest.4BC8C8F0B0ADFCA2.quest_desc: ["A MekaSuit/Meka-Tool module installed at the Modification Station."]
	quest.4BC8C8F0B0ADFCA2.quest_subtitle: "MekaSuit \\& Meka-Tool"
	quest.4BC8C8F0B0ADFCA2.title: "Hydraulic Propulsion Module"
	quest.4BCB152BBCEB3B90.quest_desc: [
		"The Environmental Eye is very useful in theory; however, a lot of magical botanists struggle with its limited range of gauging aura in the environment around them. A simple solution to this problem is the Environmental Ocular. While working similarly to the Environmental Eye, the main difference is its much bigger gauge for aura in the area: It is twice as large."
		""
		"Refer to the Book of Natural Aura (guidebook) for full detailed information on Nature's Aura."
	]
	quest.4BD1385340E3C938.quest_desc: [
		"Ore can be mined into raw ore, or smelted directly into ingots."
		""
		"In addition to regular crafting recipes, iron ingots are used to make compressed iron ingots. Throw some iron ingots on the ground and set off an explosion (i.e. TNT or mini TNT) nearby. You will lose about 20% of your ingots, but the rest will be converted to compressed iron! Later, you can make it in more efficient ways."
	]
	quest.4BD51E857E3CFC26.quest_desc: ["Build the complete Chipped suite: §6Botanist Workbench§r, §6Alchemy Bench§r, §6Carpenter's Table§r, §6Loom Table§r, §6Mason Table§r, and §6Tinkering Table§r. Every material category, covered."]
	quest.4BD51E857E3CFC26.quest_subtitle: "Chipped"
	quest.4BD51E857E3CFC26.title: "The Full Workshop"
	quest.4BDA60A93E629E04.quest_desc: [
		"Higher tier versions of the tier 1 block gen. Faster yields! "
		""
		"This block generator has a speed of 2"
	]
	quest.4BDCE44893B5E2C4.quest_desc: ["You've found your footing with fire, essence, and power. Keep climbing."]
	quest.4BDCE44893B5E2C4.quest_subtitle: "Tier 2 Trial"
	quest.4BDCE44893B5E2C4.title: "Journeyman's Trial"
	quest.4C034DCEC02656A2.quest_desc: ["A §6Fiery Ingot§r is an item crafted from one Iron Ingot and one vial of either Fiery Blood or Fiery Tears. Fiery Ingots contain a magical property that causes items crafted using the ingots to acquire fiery properties."]
	quest.4C0B27AEC1BBC826.quest_desc: ["§6Basic Purifying Factory§r. Processes many items at once. Higher tiers add more slots and speed."]
	quest.4C0B27AEC1BBC826.quest_subtitle: "Extras: Factories"
	quest.4C0B27AEC1BBC826.title: "Basic Purifying Factory"
	quest.4C0BCC84EA19B14A.quest_desc: ["Click on a mob to capture it. Gotta catch them all!"]
	quest.4C180332FEA63BB3.quest_subtitle: "ExtendedAE"
	quest.4C1AA8D6EF212081.quest_desc: ["Smelt dry rubber to make plastic."]
	quest.4C5BF6150C71F18C.quest_desc: ["§6White Collector§r, tier §e14§r of §e16§r. Collectors generate EMC from light. Each tier stores more and produces faster."]
	quest.4C5BF6150C71F18C.quest_subtitle: "Project Expansion: Collectors"
	quest.4C5BF6150C71F18C.title: "White Collector [MK 14]"
	quest.4C66F5F9AE000E04.quest_desc: ["§6Absolute Washing Factory§r. An Extras-only factory type, available in the four highest tiers."]
	quest.4C66F5F9AE000E04.quest_subtitle: "Extras: Factories"
	quest.4C66F5F9AE000E04.title: "Absolute Washing Factory"
	quest.4C6B18C8D270A43E.quest_desc: [
		"XNet is an item, fluid, energy, and information transportation mod that is all about efficiency. The cable system is designed in such way that you should be able to make huge cable systems without any overhead. Cables (for example) are not tile entities and have very simply models. This makes transporting items accross a cable of 12000 blocks long just as efficient as doing it on a 5 block long cable."
		""
		"At the core of this mod is a network. A network is basically a single section of connected cables connected (via connectors) to various blocks (chests, machines, ...) and one controller. The controller is the block that does the actual work for that network."
	]
	quest.4C6B18C8D270A43E.quest_subtitle: "XNet"
	quest.4C6E023AB7291EE5.quest_desc: ["Bound across the skies of the Aether and \"borrow\" some clouds to take back with you."]
	quest.4C6E023AB7291EE5.title: "Aerclouds"
	quest.4C72C19719188E39.quest_desc: ["§6Colossal Star Ein§r. A portable EMC battery, a colossal EMC battery. Capacity climbs with each size from §eEin§r to §eOmega§r."]
	quest.4C72C19719188E39.quest_subtitle: "Project Expansion: Greater Stars"
	quest.4C72C19719188E39.title: "Colossal Star Ein"
	quest.4C73BD54224F7CC5.quest_desc: ["Uses solid fuel to create air pressure."]
	quest.4C9ADC82F706B417.quest_desc: [
		"Alchemically pure gold. Acts as a catalysator, enabling various alchemical processes."
		""
		"See The Hermetica for more details on Theurgy."
	]
	quest.4CAFFE19D6158181.quest_desc: ["Refer to the manual for Pressure Chamber setup and recipes. These items are enough to create a 3x3x3 pressure chamber. Great for starting out!"]
	quest.4CAFFE19D6158181.title: "Pressure Chamber"
	quest.4CB408FAD78D2AD5.quest_desc: ["§6Green Relay§r, tier §e10§r of §e16§r. Relays move EMC between blocks and add a bonus per second. Higher tiers transfer far more."]
	quest.4CB408FAD78D2AD5.quest_subtitle: "Project Expansion: Relays"
	quest.4CB408FAD78D2AD5.title: "Green Relay [MK 10]"
	quest.4CB6ADD18138ACC6.quest_desc: [
		"The export bus pulls items and fluids (and whatever else, given addons) from network storage and pushes them into the inventory it's touching."
		""
		"For purposes of lag reduction, if the export bus has not exported something recently, it goes into a sort of \"sleep mode\" where it operates slowly, and wakes up and accelerates to full speed (4 operations per second) when it successfully exports something."
		""
		"They are cable subparts."
	]
	quest.4CB8D287F34ACC56.quest_desc: ["§bQuantum armor§r boots. Holds ability cards and draws power from your ME network."]
	quest.4CB8D287F34ACC56.quest_subtitle: "Advanced AE"
	quest.4CC50B32C8780595.quest_desc: ["§6Advanced Combining Factory§r. Processes many items at once. Higher tiers add more slots and speed."]
	quest.4CC50B32C8780595.quest_subtitle: "Extras: Factories"
	quest.4CC50B32C8780595.title: "Advanced Combining Factory"
	quest.4CE5621AB71CE988.quest_desc: [
		"- Place your Factory Manager in the world, and connect it to your inventories using Inventory Cables"
		"- Place the Program Disk inside the Manager's GUI"
		"- Paste your script into the manager GUI using the buttons or by using Ctrl+V"
		"- The manager should tell you that the script was loaded"
		"- Hover over the disk to see the warnings and errors for your program"
		"- Shift-right-click the manager with the label gun in your hand to load the labels from your program"
		"- You can now use the scroll wheel while holding shift to change the active label."
		"- Right click blocks in the world to apply or remove the label."
		"- There is also a right-click menu for entering a custom label that may not be in your program yet."
		"- Once you've assigned the labels, right click the manager while NOT holding shift to save the labels to the Program Disk"
		"- Your program should now be running without any issues"
	]
	quest.4CE5621AB71CE988.title: "Factory Manager Tools"
	quest.4CE60F732C4426A3.quest_desc: [
		"Super Factory Manager is a mod for Minecraft that lets users create programs to run their factories. The mod provides a domain specific-language tailored for moving items, fluids, and other resource types. A text editor is included, along with example programs."
		""
		"To get started, you will need a factory manager, a label gun, and a disk. Refer to the project page and GitHub to learn more!"
	]
	quest.4CEC846A1DD5DB84.quest_desc: [
		"Pattern providers are the primary way in which your autocrafting system interacts with the world. They push the ingredients in their patterns to adjacent inventories, and items can be inserted into them in order to insert them into the network. Often a channel can be saved by piping the output of a machine back into a nearby pattern provider (often the one that pushed the ingredients) instead of using an ME Import Bus to pull the output of the machine into the network."
		""
		"Of note, since they push the ingredients directly from the crafting storage in a crafting CPU, they never actually contain the ingredients in their inventory, so you cannot pipe out from them. You have to have the provider push to another inventory (like a barrel) then pipe from that."
		""
		"Also of note, the provider has to push ALL of the ingredients at once, it can't push half-batches. This is useful to exploit."
		""
		"Pattern providers have a special interaction with interfaces on subnets: if the interface is unmodified (nothing in the request slots) the provider will skip the interface entirely and push directly to that subnet's storage, skipping the interface and not filling it with recipe batches, and more importantly, not inserting the next batch until there's space in the machine. This works correctly with blocking mode, the provider will monitor the slots in the machine for ingredients, instead of the slots in the interface."
	]
	quest.4CFFA19AA2AA47CD.quest_desc: ["Catalysts are used in complex crafting recipes. They get harder to craft as they move higher in tiers."]
	quest.4D1BF4F802916D45.quest_desc: ["A sword with 7 attack damage."]
	quest.4D1EE9BC7F478C29.quest_desc: ["The boots of the MekaSuit."]
